<figure class="method-figure" data-gin aria-labelledby="gin-title">
  <figcaption id="gin-title"><span>Figure 2</span> The same keys answer different questions</figcaption>
  <div class="figure-options"><label>Predicate <select data-predicate><option value="contains">Contains both tags · @&gt;</option><option value="equal">Equals this array · =</option></select></label></div>
  <p class="figure-query" data-live data-query>tags @&gt; ARRAY['gift', 'ceramic']</p>
  <div class="gin-flow">
    <div class="gin-items"><p class="panel-label">Stored arrays</p>
      <div data-row="P7"><b>P7</b><code>gift, ceramic</code><span data-result data-live>not searched</span></div>
      <div data-row="reversed"><b>reversed</b><code>ceramic, gift</code><span data-result data-live>not searched</span></div>
      <div data-row="extra"><b>extra</b><code>gift, ceramic, sale</code><span data-result data-live>not searched</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓ extract keys · search their lists ↓</div>
    <div class="gin-postings"><p class="panel-label">GIN keys → posting lists of row locators</p>
      <div data-key="ceramic"><b>ceramic</b><span>P7 · reversed · extra</span></div>
      <div data-key="gift"><b>gift</b><span>P7 · reversed · extra</span></div>
      <div data-key="sale"><b>sale</b><span>extra</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="candidate" data-live data-candidates>Candidate locations: none collected</div>
  </div>
  <p data-explanation data-live aria-live="polite">The three arrays contain the same two search keys. Only P7 equals the query array.</p>
  <div class="figure-controls" role="group" aria-label="Figure 2 playback"><button data-play>Play</button><button data-back>Back</button><button data-next>Next</button><button data-reset>Reset</button><span data-step>1 / 4</span></div>
  <div data-hold aria-hidden="true"><span></span></div>
  <p class="figure-note">P7 uses its established gift/ceramic tags. “reversed” and “extra” are diagnostic arrays in a separate test table, not new catalogue products. Labels stand in for heap locators. Arrays are non-null and one-dimensional.</p>
  <details><summary>All stages, as text</summary><ol><li>Extract the component keys from each array. Each key has a list of row locators.</li><li>Look up gift and ceramic. Both lists contain all three rows.</li><li>Combine the lists: all three rows have both keys.</li><li>Containment accepts all three. Equality must check the original arrays; it rejects the reversed order and the extra element, leaving P7.</li></ol></details>
</figure>
<script>
  import { stepper } from '../figures/stepper.mjs';
  document.querySelectorAll('[data-gin]').forEach(root => {
    const select = root.querySelector('[data-predicate]') as HTMLSelectElement;
    const rows = [...root.querySelectorAll('[data-row]')];
    const player = stepper(root, { steps: () => 4, draw: step => {
      const eq = select.value === 'equal';
      root.querySelector('[data-query]').textContent = `tags ${eq ? '=' : '@>'} ARRAY['gift', 'ceramic']`;
      root.querySelectorAll('[data-key]').forEach(el => el.classList.toggle('chosen', step >= 1 && el.getAttribute('data-key') !== 'sale'));
      root.querySelector('[data-candidates]').textContent = step < 2 ? 'Candidate locations: none collected' : 'Candidate locations: P7 · reversed · extra';
      rows.forEach(el => {
        const rejected = eq && step === 3 && el.getAttribute('data-row') !== 'P7';
        el.classList.toggle('chosen', step >= 2 && !rejected);
        el.classList.toggle('rejected', rejected);
        el.querySelector('[data-result]').textContent = step < 2 ? 'not searched' : step === 2 ? 'has both keys' : rejected ? 'recheck: reject' : eq ? 'recheck: equal' : 'containment: match';
      });
      root.querySelector('[data-explanation]').textContent = [
        'Each array supplies component keys. Their order and any extra elements are not proved by finding gift and ceramic.',
        'Look up gift and ceramic. Each posting list names all three rows. The sale list is not needed for this search.',
        'Intersect the two posting lists. All three row locations survive; each row contains both search keys.',
        eq ? 'Equality checks the original arrays. Reversed order and an extra element both fail. Only P7 is equal.' : 'For this non-null containment query, array_ops can confirm all three matches from key membership. No operator recheck is required on an exact bitmap.'
      ][step];
    }});
    select.addEventListener('change', player.render);
  });
</script>
